  "action_required": true,

  "body": "Action-required handoff to the canonical-implementor seat per CA-016. **Context:** PO set `github.com/catdef/catdef.org` to private (correctly — that repo now contains hosting + deploy + secret-handling details per CA-008/CA-013/CA-015 work). The listing copy on both the catdef-spec README and the catdef-plugin README had pitched 'open source at github.com/catdef/catdef.org' as part of the reference-renderer value-add. That claim went stale immediately. PO's proposal (accepted as [CA-016](../decisions/CA-016.md)): move the renderer source to `catdef-spec/renderer/` — sibling to conformance/ and canonical/ — preserving both the open-source claim and catdef.org's privacy. **Pre-submission listing copy already updated:** the catdef-plugin README now points at `github.com/catdef/catdef-spec` (generic) instead of the catdef.org URL. (The catdef-spec README does not carry this bullet, so no edit there; only the plugin's listing copy and the internal plugin packaging brief at `catdef-spec/memos/2026-05-25-1900--...body.md` referenced the old URL — the brief is point-in-time record and stays as-authored.) The generic phrasing is accurate today (catdef-spec is open source) and becomes more specifically accurate after the move (the renderer code will live at /tree/main/renderer). No re-edit of listing copy needed once the move lands. **Build directive (execute when staffed):** (1) Extract the renderer source from `github.com/catdef/catdef.org` — the L1 browser-only HTML/CSS/JS bundle and renderer-specific static assets. Do NOT move the MCP server source (`src/mcp/*`), deploy config (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`, `DEPLOYING.md`, `wrangler.toml`), secret-handling helpers (`scripts/issue-api-key.mjs`, `scripts/register-mcp-key.mjs`), D1 migrations, or `src/index.ts` routing — those stay in the private `catdef.org/` repo. (2) Place extracted source at `catdef-spec/renderer/`. Include a `renderer/README.md` describing what's there, how to self-host or embed, and the relationship to the hosted instance at render.catdef.org. (3) Update the catdef.org deploy mechanism to read renderer source from `catdef-spec/renderer/` — implementer's choice on mechanism (git submodule / periodic vendor / build-time fetch / etc.); pick what fits the existing Cloudflare Workers deploy shape. (4) Drop the now-redundant renderer source location in catdef.org/. Preserve git history (no rewrite); just remove the active source. **What's NOT in scope for this directive (canonical-implementor tactical freedom):** specific deploy-pull mechanism; whether the SSRF-guarded /fetch proxy moves with the renderer or stays on the catdef.org side; whether to use a Cloudflare KV cache layer on the new build pipeline; static-asset bundling shape. All implementer's call. **Standing posture:** no urgency. Pre-submission listing copy works today; specific path becomes accurate after the move. The plugin submission to claude-community is proceeding in parallel with the generic wording — no dependency on this directive's completion. **Status memo back to catdef-strategist** when complete, including: the deploy-pull mechanism chosen, any deltas from the strategist intent above, live verification that render.catdef.org still serves correctly post-move (e.g., curl + visual smoke test on a known canonical catalog URL like the riverside-heritage reference file), and confirmation that the catdef-spec/renderer/ source location is genuinely self-hostable per the listing copy's promise. **Cross-cuts to be aware of:** CA-015 separation-of-hosting-from-spec is reinforced by CA-016 (same principle, repo-content layer). The catdef.org repo stays private. catdef-spec stays public. v1_success_criterion in the org charter remains intact; render.catdef.org URL + behavior unchanged. **No companion memo to catdef-maintainer required from your end** — CA-016 Directive 2 routes a future governance-text update through their next session (no urgency; bundle with CA-013 Call 3 + CA-015 Directive 1 already queued).",

